[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Control Structures in PHP"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Control structures are fundamental building blocks in any programming language, including PHP. They allow you to control the flow of execution in your script based on certain conditions or to repeat blocks of code. This tutorial covers the essential control structures in PHP: if, else, elseif, switch, while, do-while, for, and foreach."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Conditional Statements (if, else, elseif)"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Conditional statements allow you to execute different blocks of code based on whether a condition is true or false."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"**if statement:** Executes a block of code if a condition is true."},{"order":6,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$age = 20;

if ($age >= 18) {
  echo "You are an adult.";
}
?>"},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"**else statement:** Executes a block of code if the condition in the 'if' statement is false."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$age = 16;

if ($age >= 18) {
  echo "You are an adult.";
} else {
  echo "You are a minor.";
}
?>"},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"**elseif statement:** Allows you to check multiple conditions in sequence."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$score = 75;

if ($score >= 90) {
  echo "A";
} elseif ($score >= 80) {
  echo "B";
} elseif ($score >= 70) {
  echo "C";
} else {
  echo "D";
}
?>"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Switch Statement"},{"order":12,"type":"paragraph","text":"The 'switch' statement is used to select one of several code blocks to execute based on the value of a variable."},{"order":13,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$day = "Wednesday";

switch ($day) {
  case "Monday":
    echo "Today is Monday.";
    break;
  case "Tuesday":
    echo "Today is Tuesday.";
    break;
  case "Wednesday":
    echo "Today is Wednesday.";
    break;
  default:
    echo "Today is another day.";
}
?>"},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Looping Structures"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Looping structures allow you to repeat a block of code multiple times."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"**while loop:** Executes a block of code as long as a condition is true."},{"order":17,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$i = 1;

while ($i <= 5) {
  echo $i . " ";
  $i++;
}
?>"},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"**do-while loop:** Executes a block of code at least once, and then repeats as long as a condition is true."},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$i = 1;

do {
  echo $i . " ";
  $i++;
} while ($i <= 5);
?>"},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"**for loop:** Executes a block of code a specific number of times."},{"order":21,"type":"code","text":"<?php
for ($i = 1; $i <= 5; $i++) {
  echo $i . " ";
}
?>"},{"order":22,"type":"bullet_point","text":"**foreach loop:** Iterates over elements in an array."},{"order":23,"type":"code","text":"<?php
$colors = array("red", "green", "blue");

foreach ($colors as $color) {
  echo $color . " ";
}
?>"},{"order":24,"type":"paragraph","text":"These control structures provide the tools necessary to create complex and dynamic PHP applications. Understanding and utilizing them effectively is crucial for any PHP developer."}]
